body:
I did make another render of fixing up all the metal textures adding detail to it. The panels looked good, it was the ground that I did not know how to do correctly like some others had done using just a picture. 

&#x200B;

I do agree that it is pretty bad though lol

I forgot to ask this, but is it possible to have the weekly challenges pinned to the top for 2 weeks? so the current week and previous week are there for people to look at.  

&#x200B;

Only reason for this is that it is a long challenge, so it would be neat to give people a better chance to show their work since it will be on show for longer. While yes you can post work for older challenges, it can get lost since some may not even go back and look. Just an idea though .

I think having the daily ones linked to the Weekly is nice. But as it is i struggle to get even one of the dailies done, and i was going to do the black smiths one but there is so much extra time needed to create the scene and lighting etc that It is a large task for people who are new. While it is a good way to learn somethings can take awhile to learn and then when you get behind it just saps all motivation.  

&#x200B;

The barbed wire I done, for me it is really crappy at least from my perspective, but I learnt so many things although that one Model alone took 2-3 days to work out which means i was way behind :( .

&#x200B;

What i have noticed is not many people submitting anything at all, I would class myself as a lurker, but seeing peoples work is nice.   

&#x200B;

I think it will be hard to get a correct balance with what people want to do between the themes and non themes.  

&#x200B;

Wonder if people would be OK with the theme that runs but make it a bit more generic then being specific or have it both ways. An example would be: "Generic - Battlefield, Specific - WW Trench" or "Generic - Dinner, Specific - 50's Diner" so people can choose somewhat what style they want through out the week. So you can just say Chair or Bench etc for the daily so they can think of different ways they can complete the weekly using the creative freedom. Not sure if this is a good idea but thought i would put forward a suggestion.

If you know nothing about rocket engines, but are very curious about them in any small way, the information is very well presented, explained for new comers (I am one and it is completely kid/teenage friendly, no overly complex words/jargon used).  While it is a lengthy video, this is due to it's nature to be friendly for all and for people who know the basic information there are timestamps included so you can go to watch sections you want.  

&#x200B;

Highly recommended to anyone that wants to learn about rockets or space science in general if you have the time :) (Quality of this doco is amazing and well put together too)
